1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,351
AI;DR,

2
00:00:01,351 --> 00:00:03,499
version 0.1.0.

3
00:00:03,499 --> 00:00:05,694
Our first public release.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,750
Every story now has its own page,

5
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:09,725
with a short link,

6
00:00:09,725 --> 00:00:10,781
its key sources,

7
00:00:10,781 --> 00:00:11,838
and a card that's

8
00:00:11,838 --> 00:00:13,627
made for sharing.

9
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,380
You can get the digest

10
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,390
wherever you read:

11
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:18,317
on Telegram in two languages,

12
00:00:18,317 --> 00:00:19,223
by email,

13
00:00:19,223 --> 00:00:21,700
or in every new Chrome tab.

14
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,647
And it reads anywhere.

15
00:00:23,647 --> 00:00:25,168
There's an RSS feed,

16
00:00:25,168 --> 00:00:26,584
and AI agents can

17
00:00:26,584 --> 00:00:28,500
pull the news over MCP,

18
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,200
no account needed.

19
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:34,701
We went from 3 sources to 25,

20
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,978
and when many outlets

21
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:37,522
cover a story,

22
00:00:37,522 --> 00:00:40,200
they merge into one row.

23
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:41,915
The data page shows

24
00:00:41,915 --> 00:00:43,041
the whole pipeline:

25
00:00:43,041 --> 00:00:43,772
every run,

26
00:00:43,772 --> 00:00:45,003
the models doing the work,

27
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:47,198
and the tokens they use.

28
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,751
That's 332 commits in three weeks.

29
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:57,043
Read it at aidr.today.
